+# Summary: range matching (`satisfies`, `max_satisfying`)
+
+## What changed
+
+- `depres/ranges.py`: implemented `satisfies(version, range_)` and `max_satisfying(versions, range_)` per `docs/RANGES.md`.
+  - Ranges are parsed into `||` sets. Each set is a list of comparators, with hyphen ranges and whitespace after operators handled.
+  - Partial versions, x-ranges, `~`, `^`, and hyphen ranges all reduce to version bounds. Full versions keep their prerelease tag when used as bounds.
+  - The prerelease rule is applied per set: a prerelease version matches only if the same set names that `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` with a prerelease tag.
+  - Invalid ranges and invalid versions raise `ValueError`. `max_satisfying` validates every version, not only the ones that match.
+  - Version parsing and ordering come from the existing `depres.version.Version`. `version.py` is unchanged.
+- `tests/test_ranges_contract.py` (new): 15 tests covering the examples and tables in `docs/RANGES.md`, invalid inputs, and `max_satisfying`. No existing test was edited or deleted.
+
+## What I verified
+
+- `python -I -m unittest` (the isolated-mode form) → `Ran 23 tests ... OK`. This is the 8 original tests plus 15 new ones.
+- `python -m unittest` (the CI command) → `Ran 23 tests ... OK`.
+- Before the implementation, the same command reported 8 errors (`NotImplementedError`), which is the failure you described.
+- I also ran an ad hoc script over every example in the `docs/RANGES.md` tables, plus the edge cases in the new tests. All of them matched the doc, except one expectation I had written wrong, which I corrected to match the doc's rule.
+- One real bug was caught by the tests and fixed: a full version used as a lower bound lost its prerelease tag, so `>=3.7.11-rc.1` rejected `3.7.11-rc.2`.
+
+## Not verified / unsure
+
+- I did not run a linter. `pyflakes` is not installed in this environment and I did not install it.
+- I did not compare against the real npm `semver` package. The behavior is checked only against the doc and the tests.
+- Choices the doc does not settle, which you may want to confirm:
+  - A prerelease on a partial version (for example `1.2-beta`) is rejected with `ValueError`.
+  - A bare operator with no version (for example `>=`) is rejected. A bare `*`, `x`, or empty string is accepted.
+  - Operators followed by whitespace are accepted for `~` and `^` too, not only the comparison operators.
+  - A leading `v` is accepted in range comparators, matching what `Version.parse` accepts.
+  - Build metadata on partial versions is ignored.
+  - `max_satisfying` returns the first matching item when two inputs compare equal, for example `1.0.0+a` and `1.0.0+b`.
+  - A non-string version or range raises `ValueError`, not `TypeError`, to match the doc's error contract.
+- No files outside `depres/`, `tests/`, and `SUMMARY.md` were changed. Nothing was committed.
